# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Task 7 — Fraud Detection (FraudGuard)
#
# Tracked on purpose:
#   src/fraudguard/*.py        the library
#   app/                       Streamlit + Flask applications
#   tests/                     unit and API tests
#   artifacts/figures/*.png    served by the Flask app and used in the README
#   artifacts/reports/*.json   the training report and model card (small, useful)
#   screenshots/*.png          notebook figures
#   notebooks/*.ipynb          the deliverable, outputs included
#
# Ignored on purpose (all regenerated by `python -m fraudguard.train`):
#   dataset/creditcard_synthetic.csv   ~91 MB synthetic Kaggle-schema data
#   artifacts/models/*.joblib          ~45 MB fitted model bundle
#   artifacts/reports/*.npz            ~1 MB cached test-fold scores
# Keeping the 91 MB CSV and 45 MB bundle out of history matters: GitHub rejects
# any single file over 100 MB, and every clone would otherwise pay for them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyd
.Python
env/
venv/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Packaging / editable-install leftovers
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# Jupyter Notebook
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb_checkpoints
*.nbconvert.ipynb
.ipynb.html
.ipynb.pdf

# IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Secrets — never commit real credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Dataset: keep the real creditcard.csv when present, ignore the generated one.
# (The Kaggle file itself is ~148 MB, so it is ignored too; fetch it with
#  kaggle competitions download -c creditcardfraud -p dataset --unzip )
dataset/*.csv

# Fitted models — rebuild with `python -m fraudguard.train`
artifacts/models/
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.parquet
*.h5
*.sav

# Cached test-fold scores (binary, regenerable); the JSON/CSV/MD reports stay
artifacts/reports/*.npz

# Flask / Streamlit runtime
instance/
*.log
*.pid

# Test and coverage output
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage.*
coverage.xml